  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a user, I want every sheet and the image viewer to close with the system close button at the same place, so that dismissing a panel works the same everywhere and as in other iOS 27 apps. Today nine sheets use a text button « Fermer », one of them on the trailing (confirm) side, where legacy used an `xmark` symbol.\n\n### Rule\n\n- \"Use the standard Back and Close buttons. […] Prefer the standard symbols for each, and don't use a text label that says Back or Close.\" — [HIG › Toolbars](https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/toolbars) (Navigation; page updated 2025-12-16).\n- \"In iOS and iPadOS, for sheets with a single view, the Cancel button belongs on the leading edge of the top toolbar. When present, the Done button belongs on the trailing edge.\" — [HIG › Sheets](https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/sheets) (iOS, iPadOS; updated 2026-03-24).\n- API: [`ButtonRole.close`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/swiftui/buttonrole/close) (iOS 26.0+).\n\n### What the app does (dev-swift @ `7a61018f`)\n\n`ToolbarItem(placement: .cancellationAction) { Button(\"Fermer\") { dismiss() } }` at:\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Reader/Viewer/ImageViewerView.swift:27`\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Reader/VideoPlayerSheet.swift:38`\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Polls/PollSheet.swift:57`\n- `App/SwiftHFR/FilteredPosts/FilteredPostsView.swift:125`\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Smileys/SmileyPickerView.swift:61`\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Composer/Gif/GifPickerView.swift:26`\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Composer/ArchivedDraftsView.swift:27`\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Profile/UserProfileView.swift:23`\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Composer/ImageUpload/ImageUploadView.swift:33`: the same close action, but in `.confirmationAction` (trailing side).\n\nThe app is not consistent with itself: `Reader/ReaderPageSheet.swift:97` already uses `Button(\"Fermer\", systemImage: \"xmark\")`.\n\n### Legacy at `87fe0d1c`\n\n- Composer panels: `HFRswift/Swift/AnswerView.swift:1825-1848` (`ComposerSheetCloseHeader`): an `xmark` symbol on the leading edge, « Fermer » for VoiceOver only.\n- Image viewer: `HFRswift/Swift/MessagesView.swift:6749-6760`: an `xmark` button (44×44), and a drag down dismisses it (`:6683-6697`). SwiftHFR's viewer has neither (`ImageViewerView.swift:7`: \"no drag-to-dismiss\").\n- Poll: `HFRswift/Swift/PollView.swift:149` already has the text button (shared gap).\n\n### Class\n\n**(a) defect** (parity: legacy's panels and viewer use the symbol; the poll sheet alone is a shared gap).\n\n### Proposed fix and check\n\n- One shared close toolbar item: `Button(role: .close) { dismiss() }` in `.cancellationAction`, used by the ten sheets (one shared component, one pass, per #836).\n- Check: no `Button(\"Fermer\")` left in a toolbar; VoiceOver still reads « Fermer ».\n- Mac check: each sheet shows the system close symbol on the leading edge; whether the viewer gets the swipe-down back is the operator's call (#1070: system behaviour only).\n\nFound by #866 (cloud/r866-fable, Fable 5.2)",
